as even on a count despite everything before it. This was GPT-6.1 Sol's best moment, and the engine's choice here was C9."}, {"turn": 38, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's C8 gave the game back. It lost 16.2 points and sent the lead from +10.1 to +26.2, where the engine wanted B8. The rest of the game stayed within a point of +26 and ended in two passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran was a helper: current-position-liberties.js (inspectLiberties) only parses the board text and lists chains with their distinct liberties, the regions function flood-fills empty regions and their borders, and the rest was reading past game notes, calling choose_opponent and play, building the SGF from the move history, and writing notes. None of it generates, scores or ranks candidate moves or looks ahead, so the moves were chosen by the player.", "stop": false}}